<header class="vc-topbar">
    @* Grouped with the title so the header keeps two flex children: adding the
       toggle as a third would push the page title to the middle of the bar. *@
    <div class="vc-topbar__lead">
        @* Below 1024px _Sidebar is an off-canvas drawer, so without this button the
           navigation is unreachable. aria-controls names the element it opens;
           site.js keeps aria-expanded and body.nav-open in sync. *@
        <button class="vc-icon-btn vc-topbar__menu" type="button" id="vc-nav-toggle"
                aria-controls="vcSidebar" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Open navigation">☰</button>
        <div>
            <h1 class="vc-topbar__title">@ViewData["Title"]</h1>
            @if (ViewData["Subtitle"] != null)
            {
                <p class="vc-topbar__subtitle">@ViewData["Subtitle"]</p>
            }
        </div>
    </div>
    @* The bell and the gear are gone. Neither did anything when clicked: the badge
       they showed was never fed (no script reads #vc-notification-badge), while the
       live alerts themselves arrive as toasts drawn by notifications.js at the bottom
       of the screen. The gear was a disabled placeholder. A control that advertises a
       count it cannot produce is worse than no control, so the whole actions cluster
       was removed rather than left half-alive. *@
</header>